>> title: Chicken Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: chicken, mayonnaise, poached, sandwich filling, make-ahead
>> counters: Deli
>> aka: deli chicken salad, chicken mayo, tarragon chicken salad, chicken salad spread
>> pairs-with: mayonnaise, white-sandwich-bread, chicken-broth
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> step.1: poach the breasts 15 min, rest 10 min in the pot
>> step.2: dice into half-inch pieces
>> step.3: whisk the dressing
>> step.4: fold in the celery and scallion
>> step.5: chill 1 hr

Poach @boneless chicken breasts{1 1/2%lb}(680 g) in @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @bay leaf{1} and @black peppercorns{1%tsp}: bring it barely to a tremble, ~poach{15%min}, then take the pot off the heat and ~rest{10%min} with the chicken still in the liquid.

Dice @&(~1)poached chicken{} into half-inch pieces once it is cool enough to handle.

Whisk @mayonnaise{3/4%cup}(180 mL), @Dijon mustard{2%tsp}, @lemon juice{1%Tbs}, @fresh tarragon{1%Tbs}(chopped), @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} together.

Fold @&(~1)dressing{} through @&(~2)diced chicken{} with @celery{2%ribs}(diced small) and @scallions{3}(sliced thin).

Chill @&(~1)chicken salad{} ~chill{1%hr} before serving.
